---
title: Chicken Scaloppini
author: Mildred McKinzie
category: Meat, Poultry, Fish
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@boneless, skinless chicken breasts{3} (halved)
@eggs (lightly beaten){2}
@seasoned bread crumbs{1%c}
@wafer-thin slices of lemon{6}
@thin slices of Swiss cheese{6}
@lemon juice{1/2%c}
@butter{3%Tbsp}
@oil{3%Tbsp}
@heavy cream{1%c}
@flour

Preheat oven to 350 degrees. Dip chicken in lemon juice, pat with flour, then dip in beaten egg and crumbs. Heat @butter{3%Tbsp} and @oil{3%Tbsp} in heavy skillet and brown chicken on one side. Remove and place chicken cooked side down in ovenproof baking dish. Cover each piece with a slice of lemon and a slice of cheese. Pour cream over top and bake 20-30 minutes until cheese melts and cream bubbles.
